{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The protected observation `y` is a top-level data variable and is observed exactly once with a plain built-in sampling statement, after all parameters have received their built-in prior sampling statements. The predictor `x` and size `N` are context inputs and are not protected.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=1> N;
  vector[N] x; // Rainfall in cm
  vector[N] y; // Income in k$
}

parameters {
  real alpha;          // k$
  real beta;           // k$ / cm
  real<lower=0> sigma; // k$
}

model {
  alpha ~ cauchy(0, 1);
  beta ~ cauchy(0, 1);
  sigma ~ cauchy(0, 1);
  y ~ normal(beta * x + alpha, sigma);
}

","data_safe_json":"{
  "N": 2,
  "x": [
    4.484073047884468,
    2.8695671444010333
  ],
  "y": [
    2.0,
    2.0
  ]
}
","protected_variables":["y"]}
